node_modules/
web/dist/

# The database is built by `bun run api` from db/schema.lite — never committed.
db/*.db
db/*.db-shm
db/*.db-wal
db/audit/

# One shop is one FILE (`tenancy { strategy database }`), and the fleet is a
# directory of them plus the registry that indexes it. Built by the API on
# first boot — `bun run reset` removes both.
db/shops/
db/shops-registry.db*
api/src/emails/.preview/

# Object storage for File columns — written by the seed from db/seed-media/,
# which IS committed. Ignoring only the destination keeps the source in git and
# the derived bytes out.
db/public/

# The JSON Schema, regenerated by `fli db:push` and `fli db:jsonschema`. Derived
# and meant to be copied OUT — into an editor, a validator, a client generator —
# so it is not committed: nothing gates it (it is not a `*.snapshot.*`, so the
# snapshots phase never rechecks it), and `db/jsonschema.snapshot.md` beside it
# already holds the same information in the form that IS gated. A committed copy
# is a second answer that can go stale in silence.
db/.json/

# And a stray one at the old path. `litestone jsonschema` with no `--out` still
# defaults to beside the .lite — that is the library's documented default and
# fli is the layer with the opinion — so a bare run, or an editor extension
# doing the same, drops a `db/schema.json` that must not be committed back.
db/schema.json
